WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.027
JAMIE: Or it's a bet they have to
make

00:00:02.027 --> 00:00:04.053
JAMIE: regardless of the return,
because falling behind on

00:00:04.053 --> 00:00:06.080
JAMIE: compute is existential.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:07.830
RUFUS: That's the other reading.
And both can be

00:00:07.830 --> 00:00:09.470
RUFUS: true simultaneously.

00:00:09.650 --> 00:00:11.888
ALEX: Back to the wider story.
Jamie, you were

00:00:11.888 --> 00:00:14.127
ALEX: about to say something about
Llama.

00:00:14.237 --> 00:00:16.884
JAMIE: I want to know what happens
if the

00:00:16.884 --> 00:00:19.530
JAMIE: next Llama model — the one
this infrastructure

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:22.177
JAMIE: is being built for —
doesn't drive proportional

00:00:22.177 --> 00:00:24.824
JAMIE: revenue. What's the debt
service on twenty-five billion?

00:00:24.909 --> 00:00:27.894
RUFUS: We don't know the specific
rate. Bloomberg notes

00:00:27.894 --> 00:00:30.879
RUFUS: it's subject to market
interest rates and bond

00:00:30.879 --> 00:00:33.864
RUFUS: pricing conditions. But
even at a conservative estimate,

00:00:33.864 --> 00:00:36.849
RUFUS: you're talking about a
significant annual obligation.
